  "hydrated": {
    "region": {
      "id": "continent-0.province-0.region-0",
      "provisional": false,
      "name": "Ironvale",
      "description": "Nestled along the mist-laced cliffs of the Ironcoast, Ironvale is a quiet mill town where the rhythmic creak of waterwheels competes with the sigh of wind through ancient oaks. Though the land is fertile and the streams run clear, a pall hangs over the valley — not from neglect, but from memory. Locals speak in hushed tones of the Blackwood Manor, a once-grand estate now swallowed by ivy and shadow, its windows dark even at noon. No one admits to seeing the lights flicker in its upper halls… but everyone avoids the old path after sundown. The mill still turns, the baker still rises before dawn, but the air tastes of iron and old sorrow — as if the land itself remembers what the people refuse to name.",
      "rumor": "They say the lord of Blackwood Manor didn’t die — he just stopped answering the door. And every harvest moon, the millwheel turns backward… for exactly thirteen chimes.",
      "adjacentHints": [
        "The fog that clings to Ironvale’s hollows seems to thicken near the coast — where Ironcoast’s disputed borders bleed into the sea, and maps dissolve like salt in water.",
        "Travelers who’ve passed through the northern passes whisper of standing stones that hum when touched — but no one in Ironvale will confirm they exist. They just hand you an extra loaf of bread and tell you to be home before the bells toll twelve."
      ],
      "climate": "temperate",
      "settlementName": "Ironvale",
      "dungeonName": "Blackwood Manor",
      "digest": "Ironvale is a tempered mill town haunted not by monsters, but by silence — the kind that follows a truth too heavy to speak. Its people endure, but the manor watches, and the wheel remembers."
    },
